R . C h e n n a K r i s h n a Reddy  received his M.S. degree in 2008 and Ph.D. degree in 2014 from Sri Venkateswara University, Tirupati, Andhra Pradesh, India. Currently, he is working as a postdoctoral fellow with Prof. Xiaoming Lin from School  of Chemistry, South China Normal University. His research interests include the development of metal–organic frameworks derivatives and their applications in lithium-ion batteries.
Xiaoming Lin  received his M.S. degree in 2009 from South China Normal University and Ph.D. degree in 2012 from Sen Yat-sen University, China. He joined School of Chemistry, South China Normal University in 2013 and was promoted to Associate Professor in 2016. He worked as a visiting scholar at University of Science and Technology of China in 2017. His group aims to create unique metal–organic frameworks (MOFs) and their derivatives for electrochemical energy storage and conversion.
Akif Zeb  received his B.S. from Hazara University (2007), M.S. degrees in inorganic and analytical chemistry (2011) and in materials and surface engineering (2014) from Quaid-i-Azam University and National University of Sciences and Technology, Pakistan, respectively. He received his Ph.D. in 2018 in inorganic chemistry from University of Science and Technology of China. Currently, he works as a postdoctoral fellow with Prof. Xiaoming Lin at South China Normal University.
His research is focused on the design and development of new nanomaterials for energy storage and conversion, heterogenous catalysis and biomimetics.
Cheng‑Yong Su  is the Cheung Kong Professor of Chemistry at Sun Yat-Sen University (SYSU). He obtained his Ph.D. from Lanzhou University in 1996, joined Prof. Wolfgang Kaim’s group at Stuttgart University in 2001 as an Alexander von Humboldt Research Fellow, continued postdoctoral work with Prof. HansConrad zur Loye at the University of South Carolina in 2002, and promoted to full professor in SYSU in 2004. He is the author of over 400 peer-reviewed publications and 9 book chapters. His
current research interest is in the field of supramolecular coordination chemistry and materials, focusing on metal–organic materials, catalysis and nanoscience relevant to clean environment and energy.
